<text font-family="sans-serif" fill="black" x="230" y="230"
      font-size="16px" font-weight="bold">PC 01.688  More Yin-Yang</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="248">by Robert W. Strickland; 7 Oct 2015</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="266">Like Fred Van Sant's original FVS-329, 01.595,</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="284">but with 32 segments instead of 24.</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black"><tspan x="230" y="302">Angles for R.I. = 1.540</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="320">48 facets + 32 girdles</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="338">2-fold symmetry; 96 index</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="356">L/W = 1.000</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="374">P/W = 0.420 C/W = 0.182</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="392">Vol/W&#179; = 0.182</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="410">pc01688.asc</tspan>
</text>
